---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/13-04/', brochure='https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/MSD/Datasheets/volumescope-2-lifesciences-datasheet-DS0304.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Thermo Scientific VolumeScope 2 · passive stack viewer" description="Inspect a sealed VolumeScope 2 exterior and browse already-authored synthetic labels in calibrated voxel coordinates." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment vs"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/13-04/">← Equipment 13-04</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#vs-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">13-04 · DOCUMENTARY MODEL & PREAUTHORED STACK / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Thermo Scientific VolumeScope 2</h2><p>Orbit the sealed SEM console, then browse a toy stack containing two pre-labelled geometric objects. Select a cell to read its stable label and physical XYZ position. A missing plane retains its Z position.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Sealed instrument exterior</h3><div id="vs-view" aria-label="Orbitable sealed VolumeScope 2 cabinet and separate teaching desk"></div>
<div class="bar"><button data-vs-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-vs-view="shell">Console detail</button><button data-vs-view="display">Teaching display</button><button id="vs-cycle">Next stored plane</button></div>
<p id="vs-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The teal desk pad changes a stored-data view only. The instrument is inactive; nothing opens or moves.</p></section>
<section><h3>Inert toy volume</h3><canvas id="vs-plot" width="640" height="400" aria-label="Indexed synthetic shape labels on a common world-coordinate grid. Use the X and Y inputs to select a cell without clicking."></canvas>
<div class="fields"><label>Stack profile<select id="vs-profile"><option value="complete">All planes</option><option value="gap">Stored gap at index 9</option></select></label><label>Plane index<input id="vs-layer" type="range" min="0" max="13" step="1" value="5"/></label><label>X cell index<input id="vs-x" type="number" min="0" max="31" step="1" value="7"/></label><label>Y cell index<input id="vs-y" type="number" min="0" max="23" step="1" value="8"/></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="vs-inspect">Inspect recorded labels</button><button id="vs-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="vs-status" aria-live="polite">Click a cell or enter indices, then inspect the fixed stack.</p><output id="vs-result"></output><div class="bar"><button id="vs-png" disabled>Display PNG</button><button id="vs-json" disabled>Inspection JSON</button></div></section></div>
<section id="vs-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Selected configuration: Thermo Scientific <i>VolumeScope 2 SEM</i> with the sealed floor-standing column console and one 24-inch workstation monitor. The <a href={brochure+'#page=2'}>manufacturer DS0304 (2019), p. 2 product photograph</a> establishes the main silhouette; <a href={brochure+'#page=4'}>p. 4 lists the 24-inch 1920 × 1200 display</a>. The <a href="https://research.missouri.edu/sites/default/files/inline-images/Volumescope_main.jpg">installed VolumeScope 2 at the University of Missouri</a> corroborates the console and an adjacent desk. It has extra screens and room furniture not replicated here. No exterior dimensioned drawing was identified. Cabinet proportions and all enclosure/desk dimensions are estimates, not installation measurements.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original complete render of the gray base, white shroud and single monitor desk"/><figcaption>Original comparison render, not a photo. Missouri installation corroborates the relative arrangement; the desk itself is generic.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'detail.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original detail of the sealed gray chamber cover and tall white shroud"/><figcaption>Original detail compared with the vendor p. 2 photograph. Console caps, ribs and covers are purely exterior.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Independent reference</th><th>Actual / interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Active display</td><td>24 in (609.6 mm) diagonal, 16:10</td><td>Active width 516.940 mm × height 323.087 mm, targeted GLB geometry check. Console dimensions inferred and not warranted.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Grid spacing and origin</td><td>0.40 × 0.50 × 1.20 µm; lower edge (−6.4, −6.0, 2.4) µm</td><td>32 × 24 × 14 synthetic cells. Z center on index 5 is 9.00 µm.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Stable labels 17 and 35</td><td>6 × 8 × 6 voxels and (7 × 5 × 3) + (3 × 5 × 4) voxels</td><td>288 and 165 voxels (69.12 and 39.60 µm³) by direct value count.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Stored gap at plane 9</td><td>15 fewer observed cells of label 35</td><td>150 observed cells. Plane 10 stays at 15.00 µm; missing values are null, not background zero.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Register original shifted-stack acceptance</td><td>Recover alignment and preserve missing physical Z</td><td>No alignment, registration or instrument operation. Only the preauthored gap/physical Z invariant is exercised.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Fixed geometric labels use known integer ranges. Voxel-center XYZ = lower-edge origin + (index + ½) × spacing; edge bounds use full voxel footprints. The JSON export records the selected ID, raw plane labels (X fastest), physical coordinates, missing indices and observed object volume. The 3D geometry is in meters, while the unrelated toy data use µm. There are no specimens, beam controls, physical sectioning, procedures or actual measurement. This is not a SEM simulator of acquisition.</p>
<p><a href={base+'volumescope2-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'inspection-example.json'}>Output schema example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset or live hardware was tested.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/13-04/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.vs{max-width:76rem}.vs .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.vs section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.vs .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.vs .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.vs label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.vs input,.vs select,.vs button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.vs button{cursor:pointer}.vs button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.vs .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.vs #vs-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.vs #vs-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.vs #vs-plot,.vs img{width:100%;height:auto}.vs #vs-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.vs #vs-status.error{color:#a54a34}.vs .scroll{overflow:auto}.vs table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.vs td,.vs th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.vs figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.vs .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
